Z||000003||Sage||12-14-1999||09:06 AM||||Know how you feel.  I don't have a whole lot of use for the winter anymore either.  I don't live there, but I have heard that in Nevada, you have to either be independantly wealthy, or willing to serve those who are.  They seem to have taxes everywhere, but there is a lawyer out west somewhere that says he can prove income taxes are unconstitutional and vows he has never paid any, and never will!  I hear California is nice, but wall to wall people most everywhere, and again, you have to have mega bucks to be off on your own anywhere!  Don't you remember Dorothy tho?  If you can't find happiness in your own back yard, you won't really find it anywhere!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||11:38 AM||||Sage--You're pretty close to being correct about the unconstitutional income tax.  Except this is how it goes:  The only portion of the income tax that you can get away with not paying is the Social Security.  You have to file a bunch of papers with the gov.  Then you lose any gov related benefits for the rest of your life.  There are LOTS!! of them that you don't even think about.  (How about a mortgage for a mere 17%APR?  Most of the percentage rate on a mortgage is subsidized in some way by the gov.)  Sorry to get off-topic.||||reg||1
